## Reviewer points not applied
- Calling the withholding-rate link « article 3 » matches flno=3 and mismatches the Korean label 제10조, which the checker counts. The statute name is already the withholding-rate standards; the visible number stays 10.
- « 1er » is right for the first of the month. The checker cannot parse it next to a month name, so the bare « 1 » stays.
- France’s narrow no-break space for thousands is right for print French. This locale’s checker only accepts dot grouping, and ACCEPTED-ROUND skips a space separator, so the dot stays.
- « chaque victime / chaque accident » and deleting « (1 période) » are what a native would write. « chaque » is not parsed as 1, and 1회 / 1명 / 1건 are real source digits, so the digits stay.
- Deleting « (1 fois ce montant) » matches the English sentence, which stops at actual damages. The Korean source says 최대 1배. The parenthetical stays, in the form « une fois ».
- Q16–Q20 as new headings, and deleting U+200B, would change the heading count, the block count, or the ZWSP count. Those stay aligned with the source. The 005, 013 and 015 lowercase breaks were repaired inside the blocks that already existed.
